Numeric-only AI Anomaly Dashboard 

Exporter running on monitoring-vm (port 9105):
curl http://localhost:9105/metrics | grep ai_ → should show:

ai_anomaly_total

ai_anomaly_cpu_high

ai_anomaly_mem_high

Prometheus job in prometheus.yml (on monitoring-vm):

- job_name: 'ai_insights'
  static_configs:
    - targets: ['localhost:9105']


Restart Prometheus:

pkill prometheus
cd ~/prometheus-2.53.1.linux-amd64
nohup ./prometheus --config.file=prometheus.yml --web.listen-address=":9090" &


Grafana data source: Prometheus → URL http://localhost:9090 → Save & Test.

1) Create a new dashboard

Grafana → + (Create) → Dashboard → Add a new panel.

2) Panel: Total Anomalies

Data source: Prometheus

Query: ai_anomaly_total

Visualization: Stat (or Gauge)

Field → Thresholds: 0=Green, 1=Red

Title: “Total Anomalies” → Apply

3) Panel: CPU Anomaly Flag

Query: ai_anomaly_cpu_high

Visualization: Stat

Thresholds: 0=Green, 1=Red

Title: “CPU Anomaly (>80%)” → Apply

4) Panel: Memory Anomaly Flag

Query: ai_anomaly_mem_high

Visualization: Stat

Thresholds: 0=Green, 1=Red

Title: “Memory Anomaly (>85%)” → Apply

5) Save

Top-right Save → name it “AI Anomaly Dashboard”.

6) (Optional) Trigger a test to see it turn red
yes > /dev/null &     # start CPU stress
sleep 20
curl http://localhost:9105/metrics | grep ai_
pkill yes             # stop

Track B — Add “Message + Suggested Solution” (text panels)

If you want descriptive text on the dashboard:

1) Update the exporter (adds text “Info” metrics)

On monitoring-vm:

cd ~/ai-insights
source .venv/bin/activate
nano ai_anomaly_insights.py


Replace contents with:

import psutil, time
from prometheus_client import start_http_server, Gauge, Info

cpu_anom = Gauge('ai_anomaly_cpu_high', 'CPU > 80% (1=True,0=False)')
mem_anom = Gauge('ai_anomaly_mem_high', 'Memory > 85% (1=True,0=False)')
anom_count = Gauge('ai_anomaly_total', 'Total anomalies detected')

ai_message = Info('ai_anomaly_message', 'AI Insight message')
ai_solution = Info('ai_anomaly_solution', 'AI Suggested resolution')

if __name__ == "__main__":
    start_http_server(9105)
    while True:
        cpu = psutil.cpu_percent()
        mem = psutil.virtual_memory().percent
        count = 0
        msg, sol = "All systems healthy", "No action needed."

        if cpu > 80:
            cpu_anom.set(1); count += 1
            msg = f"High CPU detected ({cpu:.1f}%)"
            sol = "Check heavy processes: `top -b -n 1` or `htop`; restart offenders."
        else:
            cpu_anom.set(0)

        if mem > 85:
            mem_anom.set(1); count += 1
            msg = f"High memory usage detected ({mem:.1f}%)"
            sol = "Inspect `free -h` and services; restart non-critical ones."
        else:
            mem_anom.set(0)

        anom_count.set(count)
        ai_message.info({'message': msg})
        ai_solution.info({'solution': sol})
        time.sleep(15)


Restart it:

pkill -f ai_anomaly_insights.py || true
python3 ai_anomaly_insights.py &
curl http://localhost:9105/metrics | grep ai_anomaly_ | head


You should now see:

ai_anomaly_message_info{message="..."} 1

ai_anomaly_solution_info{solution="..."} 1

(Prometheus scrape job from Track A is already fine; no change needed.)

2) Grafana panels for text

Panel: AI Message

Add panel → Data source: Prometheus

Query: ai_anomaly_message_info

Visualization: Table (or Stat)

Transform → Add transformation → Labels to fields

Hide everything except the message field (optional)

Title: “AI Insight – Message” → Apply

Panel: Suggested Solution

Add panel → Data source: Prometheus

Query: ai_anomaly_solution_info

Visualization: Table or Text

If Table: Transform → Labels to fields, show solution

If Text (Markdown): switch to Text panel and paste:

**Suggested action:** ${__field.labels.solution}




Title: “AI Insight – Suggested Solution” → Apply

Tip: Set dashboard refresh to 10s.

Quick Troubleshooting

Grafana panel shows “No data”

Confirm exporter metrics: curl http://localhost:9105/metrics | grep ai_

Confirm Prometheus target UP: open http://<monitoring-ip>:9090/targets (see ai_insights)

Run a query in Prometheus UI: ai_anomaly_total / ai_anomaly_message_info

Panel time range: set to Last 15 minutes; refresh.
